A||||10||Tweek||How heavy is a door?||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||04-09-2001||11:16 PM||||I have to go to a junkyard tomorrow to get a door for my poor fiero. This donor car in question is placed on top of a toyota van (little larger than a vw bus) Does anyone know about how heavy those things really are? the door that is...  thanks!<P>-Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-09-2001||11:19 PM||||Power doors with glass are HEAVY!  If it just has regular windows and mirrors with no glass I would imagine its not as heavy.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-09-2001||11:19 PM||||Heavy. At least 40-50lbs.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-10-2001||07:20 AM||||More than any 40 or 50 lbs complete. It,s all I can do to to lift one. There is no good way for one person to grab the thing. If you can get someone to help you you will be better off, you don't want to risk dropping it. <P>If the donor car is on top of a van you will need a ladder and possibly rope to lower it. be careful. If the car has a sunroof you may be able to use the opening as a pully and a rope to lower it to the ground.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroparts.com||04-10-2001||07:41 AM||||74lbs without glass,skin, 95 lbs complete<BR>door.||||reg||14
Z||000005||ChadMan||04-10-2001||09:58 AM||||That sounds about right, fieroparts...I was going to guess around 100 lbs.  I found out the hard way that a complete Fiero door with power window/lock is heavy enough that you can hurt your back taking it out of the trunk of a '78 Caprice.<P>Ted, unless you're put together like Warren Sapp, you're going to need a helper to get that door down off that van.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||04-10-2001||09:58 AM||||Jeez! No wonder I had so much "fun" putting my spares under the porch. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||04-10-2001||07:17 PM||||PLEASE! NEVER NEVER work on stacked cars at the yards. They can and all to often do colapse/move without any warning at all. They can quite literally be perfectly stable looking one second and on top of you the next.<P>taking off the door won't be any fun either. You'll need at least 2-3 people to get it off the pile in any remotely safe manor.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||04-10-2001||08:21 PM||||Ask the forklift driver at the junkyard to bring the car down for you so you can get the door. <P>I knew a fiero door was heavy because I have carried one but 95-lbs? Why are these doors so heavy?<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||04-10-2001||08:48 PM||||They are heavy because they are made of case hardened steel.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||04-10-2001||10:06 PM||||a while ago someone was talking about making their fiero lighter for racing... took put the passenger seat, carpeting, AC compressor etc. and then they mentioned makiong the doors lighter.. mentioned taking out the "extra metal" in the doors.. I was like "dumbass! those are put there for safety...." I don't know if this person is on the forum now (this was a long time ago) but if they are... well.. see above. heh<P>then again, I knew of one guy who removed his back bumper (91 talon TSI) and just had the fiberglass skin on, just to get a fraction of a second shaved off his 1/4 mi. time.....<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
